    "description": "Edit a podcast filmed on several cameras: line the recordings up, tighten the episode, then cut to whoever is talking — the sound stays on the master track throughout.",
    "notes": {
      "multicam-note-intro": {
        "text": "Multicam Cut\n\nUpload the recordings of one conversation: a camera per speaker, a wide shot and the master audio (the mixer or recorder track). Audio Sync lines their clocks up, Transcribe reads the master with speaker labels, the Tighten Plan node (Cloud) trims the episode, Camera Switch (Cloud) puts each stretch on the camera of whoever is talking, and Apply Cut renders it. The sound always comes from the master; only the picture switches.\n\nDrop a file on each recording node, then Run down the chain.",
        "height": 340,
        "y": -760
      },
      "multicam-note-render": {
        "text": "The render\n\nApply Cut reads each camera at the right moment from the switched edit itself, so the cameras are not wired into it. Its Transcript output is the named transcript remapped onto the cut: wire it into an Add Captions node to caption the episode.",
        "height": 260,
        "y": -360
      }
    }
  },
