    {
      "id": "multicam-note-switch",
      "type": "sticky-note",
      "zIndex": -1,
      "position": {
        "x": 1360,
        "y": -400
      },
      "data": {
        "bold": false,
        "text": "Who is on screen\n\nCamera Switch gives speaker 1 Camera 1 and speaker 2 Camera 2 by default; open its settings to name the speakers or change their cameras. A turn shorter than the shortest shot (2.5 s) never causes a cut.\n\nLayout hints are OFF, so the edit stays cut-only: when two people talk over each other, the picture stays on the active speaker's camera, which Apply Cut renders. Turn them on only if you render through Speaker View instead.",
        "color": "#2d2d44",
        "label": "Sticky Note",
